============================================================ PART E —
REAL INTERVIEW DESIGN CHALLENGES
============================================================

These are design exercises. First identify the objects, their data,
their methods, and the rules between them. Then implement the system.

D1. BANKING SYSTEM Objects: Customer, BankAccount, Transaction
Requirements: - One customer can own multiple accounts. - Deposit and
withdrawal create transactions. - Reject invalid amounts. - Never allow
an invalid withdrawal. - Display account and transaction history.

D2. INVENTORY MANAGEMENT Objects: Product, Inventory, Supplier
Requirements: - Add and remove products. - Update stock. - Reject
selling more than available stock. - Calculate total inventory value. -
Identify low-stock products.

D3. LIBRARY MANAGEMENT Objects: Book, Member, Library Requirements: -
Add and search books. - Issue and return books. - Track availability. -
Prevent duplicate or invalid operations.

D4. TRADING PORTFOLIO Objects: Asset, Holding, Portfolio, Trade
Requirements: - Buy and sell quantities. - Track average entry price. -
Calculate invested value. - Calculate unrealized profit/loss. - Reject a
sale larger than the held quantity. - Keep a trade history.

D5. STUDENT MANAGEMENT Objects: Student, Course, GradeBook
Requirements: - Register students. - Add course marks. - Calculate
averages and grades. - Rank students. - Handle missing marks safely.

D6. E-COMMERCE SYSTEM Objects: User, Product, Cart, Order, Payment
Requirements: - Add and remove cart items. - Calculate subtotal and
discount. - Validate stock before checkout. - Create an order only after
successful validation. - Track order status.

